{"url": "https://psych.indiana.edu/graduate/how-to-apply/faqs.html", "final_url": "https://psych.indiana.edu/graduate/how-to-apply/faqs.html", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "FAQs: How to Apply: Graduate: Psychological and Brain Sciences: Indiana University Bloomington\nSkip to Content\nSkip to Main Navigation\nSkip to Search\nThe College of Arts & Sciences\nDepartment of\nPsychological and Brain Sciences\nHome\nAbout\nMission\nHistory\nEmployment\nIU Collaborative Partners\nDepartmental Awards\nAccess and Support Committee\nThe Human Brain Sculpture\nAbout Bloomington\nDirectory\nAdministration\nFaculty\nResearch Scientists\nStaff\nGraduate Students\nShops\nUndergraduate\nPsychology B.A.\nPsychology B.S.\nClinical Psychological Science B.S.\nNeuroscience B.S.\nMinor + Certificates\nCourses\nAdvising\nHonors Program\nResearch Opportunities\nFunding Opportunities\nScholarships & Awards\nStudent Experience\nCareer Preparation\nGraduate\nPh.D. Degree Specializations\nStudent Experience\nFunding Opportunities\nCareer Preparation\nHow to Apply\nPBS Award Applications\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nLabs & Resources\nDepartment News\nParticipate\nAlumni & Giving\nAlumni Awards\nEliot S. Hearst Memorial Lectureship\nGet Involved\nOutreach & Clinic\nClinic\nChild Scientists\nParticipate in Experiments\nScience Fest\nCommunity Partnerships\nNews\nNews\nEvents\nNewsletter\nSearch\nContact\nStudent Portal\nPh.D. Degree Specializations\nStudent Experience\nFunding Opportunities\nCareer Preparation\nHow to Apply\nFAQs\nPBS Award Applications\nHome\nGraduate\nHow to Apply\nFAQs\nFAQs\nFAQs about the application process\nWhat happens after I submit my application?\nOnce you submit the electronic IU application you will receive an email confirmation. Within the IU application you will complete a \"Department Questions\" section. Complete applications that arrive by the December 1 deadline will be reviewed by the appropriate faculty as well as the department's Graduate Admissions Committee.\nHow can I check the status of my application and/or recommendation letters?\nYou may log back into the IU application system. The system will indicate \"submitted\" as your status if the application has been received successfully. The status of electronic recommendation letters will also be reflected. The status does not indicate the admission decision.\nWhen will I learn the outcome of my application?\nAdmission decisions are typically sent mid-February through March. The department staff cannot release admission decisions over the phone. They will not release admission decisions via email until after the official notifications are sent.\nDo you accept the IELTS in place of the TOEFL?\nYes. If you take the IELTS you need to receive a minimum score of 6.5.\nEnglish is not my native language, but I completed my undergraduate degree in the U.S. Do I still have to take the TOEFL or IELTS?\nNo. Our admissions committee will automatically note the undergraduate degree during the review process.\nApplying to dual programs with Cognitive Science or Neuroscience?\nLet us know on our application; we will coordinate sharing your transcripts with that department. Also, you only have to pay the application fee once. To get a coupon code to waive the fee, send an email to grdschl@indiana.edu with your name, IU CAS ID, program(s) to which you are applying, and state that you are applying to a dual program.\nFaculty + Staff Intranet\nPsychological and Brain Sciences social media channels\nTwitter\nFacebook\nInstagram\nYouTube\nCollege of Arts & Sciences\nDepartment of Psychological and Brain Sciences\nThe College of Arts & Sciences\nThe College of Arts & Sciences\nAbout\nMission\nHistory\nEmployment\nFaculty Opportunities\nStaff Opportunities\nResearch Opportunities\nIU Collaborative Partners\nDepartmental Awards\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nStaff\nAccess and Support Committee\nThe Human Brain Sculpture\nAbout Bloomington\nMusic & Entertainment